    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Peds dosing:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " dexamethasone 0.6 mg/kg/d × 2 d, often preferred in the ED; prednisone or prednisolone 1–2 mg/kg/d (max 20 mg/d @ 0–2 y, 30 mg/d @ 3–5 y, 40 mg/d @ 6–11 y) for 3–5 d."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Asthma exacerbation:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " give for all but the mildest (⍉needed if PEF normalizes after 1–2 bronchodilator doses); early use often aborts the exacerbation, ↓ hsp and relapse. PO and IV are equally effective."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "IV methylprednisolone if a line = in place, switch to PO when convenient. ⍉taper needed if also on an ICS."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Contraindicated in systemic fungal infect. ⍉live vax @ immunosuppressive doses. Caution: HF, HTN, renal insuff; peptic ulcer, diverticulitis (perf risk)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "CYP3A4 inducers (phenytoin, carbamazepine, RIF, barbiturates) may require a higher steroid dose; inhibitors (ketoconazole, itraconazole, ritonavir, erythromycin) raise levels. NSAIDs/ASA: ↑ GI SE. Warfarin: response USU inhibited; monitor INR often. K-depleting diuretics: watch for hypokalemia."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Watch for infect. Long-term:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " consider osteoporosis prev (calcium, vitD, bisphos, weight-bearing exercise); use the lowest effective dose and duration."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Don't stop abruptly; taper after prolonged use (AI risk for up to 12 mo). Tell other clinicians you take steroids; seek care promptly for fever or infect."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
